.TH AICAMPRO-SETUP 1 "2026-08-20" "AICamPro 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
aicampro\-setup \- build the GPU runtime AICamPro needs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aicampro-setup
.SH DESCRIPTION
Creates a per-user Python environment under
.I ~/.local/share/aicampro/venv
and installs PyTorch built for ROCm, Qt, OpenCV and the matting models into it.
.PP
This is separate from the package because the ROCm build of PyTorch is roughly
14 GB installed \(em 13 GB of that being the ROCm libraries bundled inside the
wheel \(em and it has to match the amdgpu driver on the machine. Shipping it
inside a .deb or an AppImage is not practical.
.PP
Running it again is safe: it reuses an existing environment and skips anything
already downloaded.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ROCM_CHANNEL
PyTorch ROCm wheel index to install from. Defaults to
.IR rocm6.4 .
.TP
.B AICAMPRO_BOOTSTRAP_PYTHON
Interpreter used to create the environment. The AppImage passes its own so
that PyTorch matches the Python ABI the application runs on.
.TP
.B AICAMPRO_MODEL_DIR
Where to place the matting models.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Warns when no AMD GPU is visible, and when the invoking user is not in the
.B render
group \(em without it ROCm cannot reach the card even though the driver is
loaded.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR aicampro (1)
